	<!-- M-07: Universal Links for the Auth0 callback are NOT ACTIVE on iOS.

	     Unlike Android — which at least declares an autoVerify App Link filter —
	     nothing in this target requests Universal Links yet. There is no
	     com.apple.developer.associated-domains entitlement in
	     exchangapay.entitlements, so the custom scheme below is the ONLY callback
	     path on iOS, and any app that registers the same scheme can receive the
	     authorization code. This comment is the whole iOS half of the fix so far.

	     Two independent things are required, and neither is done:

	       1. Auth0 must serve the association file for this tenant. We do not
	          host it — Auth0 does, at
	          https://<tenant>/.well-known/apple-app-site-association — once the
	          Team ID and bundle ID are set in the Auth0 Dashboard under
	          Advanced Settings > Device Settings > iOS.

	       2. The associated-domains entitlement must be added here AND the
	          Associated Domains capability enabled on the App ID in the Apple
	          Developer portal, with provisioning profiles regenerated. Adding the
	          entitlement without the portal change does not degrade gracefully —
	          it breaks code signing for every iOS build including CI.

	     Do both in that order. Steps, verification commands and the removal
	     criteria for the scheme below: security/M07_APPLINKS_SETUP.md -->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
			<string>None</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>auth0</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<!-- Legacy custom scheme. Claimable by any app on the device, which is
				     what M-07 is about — but it is currently the only iOS callback
				     path, so removing it before Universal Links work would break login
				     entirely rather than harden it.

				     REMOVAL REVIEW DATE: 2027-02-06, matching the Android legacy
				     filter. Criteria in security/M07_APPLINKS_SETUP.md — both
				     platforms should stop depending on custom schemes together. -->
				<string>$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER).auth0</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
